    "Simulation only: valve, leak sensor, flow meter, phones, WAN and monitoring centre are models.",
    "The flow meter is an assumed extra device; many homes have none. Without it, confirmation rests on the valve's own position report.",
    "The valve's travel is modelled as a jump from open to closed (or to 40%) after 4-8 s; no intermediate positions, no water hammer, no slow seepage.",
    "A new close attempt is used to make the valve report its state again; a real hub would read the attribute (e.g. Matter ValveConfigurationAndControl CurrentState) instead.",
    "Reboot model: all hub components die together, the journal survives except unsynced records; disk corruption beyond a torn last line is not modelled.",
    "One leak per run, one valve, one household layout; people's replies and actions are not modelled.",
    "Escalation timing (30 s) and attempt timeout (10 s) are design choices, not tuned to a product.",
    "Not a certified leak-protection system. Real water shut-off must be installed and tested by qualified people."
